WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.549
INFERIVA for microfinance banks: an overview.

00:00:04.533 --> 00:00:08.792
At many microfinance banks, one person is the compliance officer,

00:00:08.792 --> 00:00:13.574
the money laundering reporting officer and, most weeks, the risk manager.

00:00:13.574 --> 00:00:15.605
They know their customers well.

00:00:15.605 --> 00:00:20.780
The examiner still asks how higher-risk customers are identified and monitored,

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:22.614
and wants to see the record.

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:28.554
INFERIVA is sized for that team: the same platform larger institutions use,

00:00:28.554 --> 00:00:31.262
set up with only what a small team needs,

00:00:31.262 --> 00:00:36.019
and judged against what an institution of your size is expected to hold.

00:00:37.033 --> 00:00:41.937
Monitoring starts with a short list of rules, each switched on deliberately,

00:00:41.937 --> 00:00:47.035
with its version on record: large cash deposits, and high transaction velocity.

00:00:48.233 --> 00:00:52.278
Alerts arrive in one queue, with the rule, the amount and the customer,

00:00:52.278 --> 00:00:54.328
so the day starts with what matters.

00:00:55.533 --> 00:00:58.610
One click shows the customer and every transaction,

00:00:58.610 --> 00:01:00.660
with its channel and counterparty,

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:05.365
so a market trader's evening deposits can be judged against their own pattern.

00:01:06.567 --> 00:01:10.492
When something needs a closer look, it becomes a case, with notes,

00:01:10.492 --> 00:01:14.297
an owner and a timeline that stay on record when people move on.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:19.200
Suspicious activity reports are drafted from the case and filed,

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:22.669
and each one is tracked until the regulator acknowledges it.

00:01:23.867 --> 00:01:28.517
Reporting deadlines, board reports and policy reviews sit in one calendar,

00:01:28.517 --> 00:01:31.345
so nothing depends on one person remembering.

00:01:32.533 --> 00:01:36.380
Rules, alerts, cases, reports and deadlines, in one place,

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:38.170
and sized for a small team.

00:01:38.170 --> 00:01:42.349
So the record shows what you already know about your customers,

00:01:42.349 --> 00:01:44.139
and an examiner can see it.

00:01:45.133 --> 00:01:48.004
To see it for your institution, talk to INFERIVA.
